WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.207 --> 00:00:03.375
southern California, another 12

00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:04.977
to 24 inches expected today.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.513
We do begin, though, in Ukraine

00:00:07.646 --> 00:00:09.748
where 48 children are among the

00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:10.949
thousands still trapped in the

00:00:10.949 --> 00:00:13.652
city of bakhmut as war rages all

00:00:13.786 --> 00:00:14.486
around them.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.821
Officials say they are urging

00:00:15.954 --> 00:00:17.156
everyone to get out, but some

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:19.758
are in areas that are no longer

00:00:19.892 --> 00:00:20.159
accessible.

00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:22.561
&gt;&gt; CNN's Alex Marquardt is in

00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:24.063
eastern Ukraine this morning.

00:00:24.196 --> 00:00:25.664
Give us a sense what is the

00:00:25.798 --> 00:00:27.332
reality there in and around

00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:29.935
bakhmut at this hour?

00:00:30.069 --> 00:00:31.203
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Well, tens of

00:00:31.336 --> 00:00:32.971
thousands of residents have left

00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:34.540
bakhmut but it is just

00:00:34.973 --> 00:00:35.474
extraordinary to think there are

00:00:35.607 --> 00:00:36.975
still that many civilians in the

00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:37.209
city.

00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:39.044
That city has just been

00:00:39.178 --> 00:00:39.445
pulverized.

00:00:39.578 --> 00:00:43.048
It is the site of the tiersest

00:00:43.182 --> 00:00:43.649
fighting in the country

00:00:43.782 --> 00:00:44.983
according to president zelenskyy

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.086
and top military commanders.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:49.354
Ukrainian forces appear to be on

00:00:49.488 --> 00:00:50.556
their heels as Russian forces

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:51.190
press forward.

00:00:51.323 --> 00:00:52.991
There has been no decision

00:00:53.058 --> 00:00:54.426
whether to pull back by the

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.861
Ukrainians, whether to surrender

00:00:55.994 --> 00:00:57.996
the city according to a military

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.998
spokesman in this part of the

00:01:00.132 --> 00:01:01.700
country, but the Russians do

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:04.536
appear to be trying to encircle

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.438
the city, they have taken some

00:01:06.572 --> 00:01:08.207
areas north of bakhmut.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.641
Those forces have been primarily

00:01:09.775 --> 00:01:14.513
made up of those mercenaries and

00:01:14.646 --> 00:01:15.647
convicts for the past few months

00:01:15.781 --> 00:01:17.282
leading that fight, they have

00:01:17.416 --> 00:01:18.450
been backed up by regular

00:01:18.584 --> 00:01:19.251
Russian forces.

00:01:19.384 --> 00:01:21.453
Now the Ukrainians say that

00:01:21.587 --> 00:01:24.590
these are the top fighters that

00:01:25.023 --> 00:01:25.524
are leading this push.

00:01:25.657 --> 00:01:28.127
We did hear from an Ukrainian

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.495
soldier yesterday who said

00:01:29.628 --> 00:01:31.096
despite the dire picture painted

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.198
by Ukrainian officials the

00:01:33.332 --> 00:01:35.934
actual situation is 100% worse.

00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:39.104
So Ukraine trying to hold on as

00:01:39.238 --> 00:01:41.039
their defensive positions get

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:41.140
pummeled.

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:42.641
If Russia were to take the city

00:01:43.041 --> 00:01:43.842
it would be a significant

00:01:43.976 --> 00:01:45.377
victory as you know we've been

00:01:45.511 --> 00:01:46.545
talking about this fight for

00:01:46.678 --> 00:01:47.479
bakhmut for months now, it would

00:01:47.613 --> 00:01:49.882
be a boost for Russia, a real

00:01:50.015 --> 00:01:51.617
blow for Ukraine.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.053
Both sides have lost thousands

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.155
of men.

00:01:56.288 --> 00:01:57.589
It would give Russia another

00:01:57.723 --> 00:02:00.092
foot hold here in the donbas, in

00:02:00.225 --> 00:02:01.927
eastern Ukraine, but Ukraine

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.063
will try to make that as much of

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.366
a symbolic victory as they can

00:02:07.499 --> 00:02:09.067
rather than a strategic victory.

00:02:09.101 --> 00:02:11.303
If Russia were to push them out

00:02:11.436 --> 00:02:12.437
Ukraine would digs in just to

00:02:12.571 --> 00:02:13.572
the west of the city and at this

00:02:13.705 --> 00:02:16.508
point in this very bloody

00:02:16.642 --> 00:02:17.376
fighting they are trying to

00:02:17.509 --> 00:02:18.410
weaken the Russian forces as

00:02:18.544 --> 00:02:19.745
much as possible so that even if

00:02:19.878 --> 00:02:21.613
they did take the city, that

00:02:21.747 --> 00:02:23.582
there wouldn't be in any kind of

00:02:23.715 --> 00:02:25.083
condition to press forward after

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:25.317
that.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.486
But the fight is still very much

00:02:27.619 --> 00:02:29.087
ongoing, Russians trying to

00:02:29.221 --> 00:02:30.122
stand their ground.

00:02:30.255 --> 00:02:32.124
Jim and Erica?

00:02:32.257 --> 00:02:33.892
&gt;&gt; Alex Marquardt, thanks so

00:02:34.026 --> 00:02:34.193
much.

00:02:34.326 --> 00:02:35.727
&gt;&gt;&gt; Joining us now to discuss

00:02:35.861 --> 00:02:39.164
retired U.S. Army major Mike

00:02:39.298 --> 00:02:39.464
Lyons.

00:02:39.598 --> 00:02:41.099
Good to have you on.

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:43.268
Thanks for faking the time this

00:02:43.402 --> 00:02:43.635
morning.

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:44.036
&gt;&gt; Hey, Jim.

00:02:44.169 --> 00:02:44.603
Great to be with you.

00:02:44.736 --> 00:02:46.004
&gt;&gt; You've been watching this

00:02:46.138 --> 00:02:47.105
battlefield closely.

00:02:47.139 --> 00:02:48.106
Ukrainian officials say they

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.243
have not yet made a decision to

00:02:51.376 --> 00:02:51.977
pull back from bakhmut, they are

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:52.744
clearly placing a lot of

00:02:53.111 --> 00:02:53.478
importance on this.

00:02:53.612 --> 00:02:55.647
There is a view that there might

00:02:55.781 --> 00:02:57.649
be room for strategic retreat as

00:02:57.783 --> 00:02:58.217
it were.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.451
What's your view?

00:02:59.585 --> 00:03:01.854
Should they hold that ground?

00:03:01.987 --> 00:03:04.489
Is it worth the price they're

00:03:04.623 --> 00:03:05.123
paying?

00:03:05.123 --> 00:03:09.261
&gt;&gt; Well, there is not a lot of

00:03:09.394 --> 00:03:11.196
evade while the enemy is strong

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.731
and Ukraine has to take a hard

00:03:13.131 --> 00:03:13.498
look at that.

00:03:13.632 --> 00:03:15.534
They cannot afford to lose young

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.169
men and women in this fight

00:03:17.302 --> 00:03:18.570
given the fact they will have to

00:03:18.704 --> 00:03:20.172
be deployed someplace else.

00:03:20.305 --> 00:03:22.174
Bakhmut does not hold any

00:03:22.307 --> 00:03:23.342
strategic value on the ground

00:03:23.475 --> 00:03:24.409
really and they have to

00:03:24.543 --> 00:03:26.778
recognize that and understand

00:03:27.145 --> 00:03:28.413
that their forces are better

00:03:28.547 --> 00:03:29.448
used elsewhere at this point.

00:03:29.581 --> 00:03:31.683
It's a hard decision, likely to

00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:33.151
take, and it would not

00:03:33.151 --> 00:03:34.453
necessarily mean retreat or a

00:03:34.586 --> 00:03:36.088
loss and let Russia do what it

00:03:36.221 --> 00:03:37.656
wants with it, but it's more of

00:03:37.789 --> 00:03:40.259
an evade when it enemy is

00:03:40.392 --> 00:03:40.626
strong.

00:03:40.759 --> 00:03:42.227
They have a lot more of that

00:03:42.361 --> 00:03:42.628
firepower.

00:03:42.761 --> 00:03:43.629
&gt;&gt; We were back once again in a

00:03:43.762 --> 00:03:45.163
space we've been many times

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.765
since the start of this war more

00:03:47.165 --> 00:03:48.634
than a year ago and that is a

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.135
new weapons system is going in,

00:03:50.269 --> 00:03:53.171
a capable one, in this case

00:03:53.171 --> 00:03:54.273
tanks such as the Lee pardons

00:03:54.406 --> 00:03:55.641
and the U.S. Made Abrams tanks

00:03:55.774 --> 00:03:57.776
but the focus is another weapons

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.511
system, this one the f-16 which

00:03:59.645 --> 00:04:01.246
U.S. Officials have said since

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.681
the beginning of the war that

00:04:02.814 --> 00:04:06.485
that's not the weapon that

00:04:06.618 --> 00:04:07.452
Ukrainian forces really need

00:04:07.586 --> 00:04:08.420
right now.

00:04:08.553 --> 00:04:09.621
I wonder do you agree with that

00:04:09.755 --> 00:04:10.555
assessment or should the U.S.

00:04:10.689 --> 00:04:12.858
And its partners send them in?

00:04:13.191 --> 00:04:15.193
&gt;&gt; No, I do agree with that.

00:04:15.193 --> 00:04:17.562
I think applying F-16s to the

00:04:17.696 --> 00:04:18.430
battlefield right now

00:04:18.563 --> 00:04:19.564
immediately, first of all, just

00:04:19.698 --> 00:04:21.199
couldn't happen, it would take

00:04:21.199 --> 00:04:22.734
nine months to a year to train

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:25.203
Ukrainian pilots to fly them and

00:04:25.203 --> 00:04:26.805
to coordinate a combined arms

00:04:27.205 --> 00:04:28.273
battlefield with tanks and

00:04:28.407 --> 00:04:29.207
communication systems and

00:04:29.308 --> 00:04:30.409
infantry on the ground would be

00:04:30.542 --> 00:04:31.209
very difficult.

00:04:31.209 --> 00:04:34.746
The F-16s, though, give Ukraine

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.848
attack capability inside of

00:04:37.215 --> 00:04:37.316
Russia.

00:04:37.316 --> 00:04:38.884
In this war of attrition right

00:04:39.217 --> 00:04:40.786
now the side that wins attacks

00:04:41.219 --> 00:04:42.120
the other side's capability to

00:04:42.254 --> 00:04:42.754
wage war.

00:04:42.888 --> 00:04:43.722
Right now Ukraine doesn't have

00:04:43.855 --> 00:04:45.223
that capability.

00:04:45.324 --> 00:04:45.657
Russia does.

00:04:45.791 --> 00:04:47.926
Russia is inside Ukraine and is

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:48.660
attacking their infrastructure.

00:04:48.794 --> 00:04:51.396
So the F-16s while they might

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.564
solve a problem in the short

00:04:52.698 --> 00:04:54.366
term, if they're there right now

00:04:54.499 --> 00:04:55.400
they're just not going to get

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:56.902
there on time and I just don't

00:04:57.235 --> 00:04:58.103
believe they will have any

00:04:58.236 --> 00:04:59.237
impact on the battlefield.

00:04:59.304 --> 00:05:01.440
&gt;&gt; I want to ask you about nato

00:05:01.573 --> 00:05:03.442
expansion last June, we were in

00:05:03.575 --> 00:05:05.877
Madrid as nato announced the

00:05:06.011 --> 00:05:08.880
accession or their support,

00:05:09.247 --> 00:05:11.683
unanimous support of Finland and

00:05:11.817 --> 00:05:12.150
Sweden joining.

00:05:12.284 --> 00:05:13.652
Since then Turkey has again

00:05:13.785 --> 00:05:15.354
stood in the way, Turk I didn't

00:05:15.487 --> 00:05:19.257
and Hungary of Sweden's

00:05:19.257 --> 00:05:19.458
accession.

00:05:19.591 --> 00:05:20.425
Finland is preparing to take

00:05:20.559 --> 00:05:21.460
steps forward.

00:05:21.593 --> 00:05:22.761
Do you think it is smart to

00:05:22.894 --> 00:05:26.131
split the two?

00:05:26.264 --> 00:05:30.936
Start with Finland, possibly

00:05:31.269 --> 00:05:31.870
move on to Sweden if the Turkish

00:05:32.004 --> 00:05:33.638
or Hungarians allow that to

00:05:33.772 --> 00:05:35.707
happen or is it better for them

00:05:35.841 --> 00:05:36.375
to go together?

00:05:36.508 --> 00:05:38.276
&gt;&gt; I think it's better for them

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:39.778
to go together.

00:05:39.911 --> 00:05:41.980
Nato has to be strong here.

00:05:42.114 --> 00:05:43.281
The Turks have a number,

00:05:43.315 --> 00:05:44.216
whatever that number is that

00:05:44.349 --> 00:05:45.884
they want concessions to make it

00:05:46.018 --> 00:05:47.352
happen, that's the down side of

00:05:47.486 --> 00:05:48.920
the alliance and the fact that

00:05:49.287 --> 00:05:51.289
each nato country has to approve

00:05:51.356 --> 00:05:52.457
acceptance into it.

00:05:52.591 --> 00:05:55.293
I was never one for bringing

00:05:55.327 --> 00:05:55.961
actually a lot of those nato

00:05:56.094 --> 00:05:56.862
countries that are close to

00:05:57.295 --> 00:05:58.497
Russia into nato in the past

00:05:58.630 --> 00:05:59.731
because we can't have membership

00:05:59.865 --> 00:06:01.666
to nato to be everybody but

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:02.868
Russia in Europe because that

00:06:03.301 --> 00:06:04.202
creates the same problem we had

00:06:04.336 --> 00:06:05.437
during the first World War and

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.838
that's what Russia -- one of

00:06:06.972 --> 00:06:08.407
Russia's sticking points to be,

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:09.841
but now the situation has

00:06:09.975 --> 00:06:11.309
changed on the ground, I think

00:06:11.309 --> 00:06:12.244
that both of them need to go in

00:06:12.377 --> 00:06:13.678
at the same time, the alliance

00:06:13.812 --> 00:06:14.679
has got to be strong.

00:06:14.813 --> 00:06:16.581
And then eventually now I could

00:06:16.715 --> 00:06:18.116
even see go five years down the

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.818
road, once there is a peace

00:06:19.951 --> 00:06:20.952
settlement that Ukraine does get

00:06:21.319 --> 00:06:22.721
more security assurances from

00:06:22.854 --> 00:06:24.589
nato eventually and maybe

